From b6b29af75fb955a601c6ffeef9bfe4e1b36ae260 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:55:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] vr: complete controller bindings, analog sticks and shoulder
 pressure

One OpenXR action per PS2 input (face buttons, Start/Select, menu tap/hold,
L1/R1/L2/R2, L3/R3, D-pad, both analog sticks, a face pad) so SteamVR's binding
UI lists and rebinds them. Default bindings per interaction profile live in
ga2_vr_bindings.h (simple, Touch, Touch Pro/Plus, Pico 4/Neo 3, HP G2, Index,
WMR/Odyssey, Vive wands); profiles that need an instance extension are
suggested only when the runtime offers it.

The action -> pad mapping is a pure class (ga2_vr_input.h): hysteresis, menu
tap = Start / hold = Select, both grips = recentre without L1/R1, stick as
analog bytes and D-pad, right stick sideways = L2/R2, face pad quadrants, and
what the triggers press by scene (click on the flat screen, Circle in 3D scenes
and on the tactical map, Cross in the cockpit, L2/R2 in the unit camera view).
ga2_vrpointer::setScene lets game hooks name the scene.

ps2_pad hands the VR sticks and the analog L1/R1/L2/R2 pressure to the pad
stub; the pressure bytes 16..19 now follow libpad's order (L1, R1, L2, R2; the
games read R1/R2 as bytes 17/19 to raise and lower the battle map camera).
Both stick clicks open the cheat menu from VR as on a gamepad.

Test aids: GA2_VR_PAD_LOG, GA2_VR_INPUT_SCRIPT, GA2_PAD_TRACE shows sticks and
pressure. Unit tests: ga2_vr_input_tests.cpp (mapper, per-profile path lists).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
